{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["And the reason for <b>“Now the man Moses was very humble”</b> — to declare that HaShem was jealous for his sake on account of his humility, for he would never plead his own cause, even though he knew. And R. Abraham ibn Ezra explains it to mean that he did not seek greatness over any person, nor would he take pride in his virtue at all, even over his brethren — and they were sinning by speaking against him without cause. But in the Sifrei (Beha'alotkha 100), Rabbi Natan says: they even spoke about him to his face, as it is stated, “And YHWH heard, and the man Moses was very humble” — rather, Moses suppressed the matter. Scripture mentions his humility, which he bore and did not answer them, and HaShem was jealous for his sake."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:04:29.837132796Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}